WEBVTT

00:06.048 --> 00:07.216
I'll fucking kill you.

00:07.299 --> 00:09.677
-[grunting]
-[intense music playing]

00:10.136 --> 00:11.011
[yelling]

00:11.095 --> 00:12.221
[Butcher] I got you something.

00:12.304 --> 00:14.014
[Ryan] Terror!
Does he still hump everything?

00:14.098 --> 00:15.224
[Butcher] He does his best.

00:15.307 --> 00:16.809
My grandma was diagnosed with leukemia.

00:16.892 --> 00:18.644
I discovered a cure.

00:18.728 --> 00:19.854
They laughed at me.

00:19.937 --> 00:22.106
Fuck them all.

00:22.189 --> 00:23.441
[Firecracker] Heavens to Betsy!

00:23.524 --> 00:26.360
What's that smell? It's Soldier Boy.
I can smell him all over you.

00:26.444 --> 00:28.779
-Where's Noir?
-He just disappears every afternoon.

00:28.863 --> 00:30.364
Won't say where he's going.
Won't say shit.

00:30.448 --> 00:31.866
-I trusted you.
-[Deep] Are you still butthurt

00:31.949 --> 00:34.368
-about me bringing in Stan Edgar?
-[Black Noir] I thought we were friends.

00:34.452 --> 00:36.787
I needed a win from Homelander,
Edgar was it.

00:36.871 --> 00:39.331
If we get the V1 first,
we save Annie, we save Kimiko.

00:39.415 --> 00:40.624
If Homelander gets it, he's immortal.

00:40.708 --> 00:42.209
[Butcher] A punch like
a bleeding sledgehammer

00:42.293 --> 00:43.878
and a taste for fucking smack.

00:43.961 --> 00:44.837
Bombsight.

00:44.920 --> 00:46.922
[Soldier Boy] Enriched uranium.

00:47.006 --> 00:48.424
Good luck getting out of a Supe-proof cell

00:48.507 --> 00:50.301
while you're bleeding out of your ass.

00:50.384 --> 00:51.719
The V1 wasn't here.

00:51.802 --> 00:53.721
Just fucking do it already.

00:53.804 --> 00:56.182
[Homelander] I was visited by an angel.

00:56.265 --> 00:58.350
Today, we commit ourselves

00:58.434 --> 01:00.978
to a divine rebranding.

01:01.061 --> 01:02.021
I am the Messiah.

01:02.104 --> 01:05.191
The Democratic Church of America!

01:05.274 --> 01:07.193
[congregation chanting] Homelander!
Homelander!

01:08.444 --> 01:09.445
[inspirational music playing]

01:09.528 --> 01:11.530
[narrator] They're up before dawn.

01:11.614 --> 01:13.991
They got a thousand
heads of cattle to herd.

01:14.074 --> 01:17.953
It's hard work and strong coffee.

01:18.037 --> 01:19.955
Old leather saddles

01:20.039 --> 01:22.583
and the worn stock of a trusty Remington.

01:22.666 --> 01:25.586
And when the sun finally rises
over the range,

01:25.669 --> 01:27.505
the cowboys know

01:27.588 --> 01:30.090
America is God's country

01:30.174 --> 01:33.176
and Americans, God's chosen people.

01:33.259 --> 01:36.055
So shouldn't we have
our own church for Americans

01:36.138 --> 01:39.517
with American grit and American values?

01:39.600 --> 01:42.436
Founded by the greatest American
of us all?

01:42.520 --> 01:45.104
A true American prophet?

01:45.189 --> 01:48.442
Come home to the
Democratic Church of America.

01:48.526 --> 01:50.694
Come home to Homelander.

01:50.777 --> 01:53.781
Already, the campaign's Aided Awareness

01:53.864 --> 01:57.243
outpaces the norm by plus-22 points,

01:57.326 --> 02:03.290
led by white men and women,
ages 36 to 54 and 55 to 72.

02:03.374 --> 02:06.961
We are also seeing massive growth
on the ground level.

02:07.044 --> 02:10.047
Yeah? 'Cause I'm seeing
massive growth myself.

02:13.884 --> 02:16.178
Church attendance is up,

02:16.262 --> 02:19.265
and our online donation CTR is at 44%.

02:19.348 --> 02:20.724
That's a new record. Amen.

02:20.808 --> 02:22.017
Amen.

02:22.101 --> 02:26.939
Next up is a 500 million ad blitz

02:27.022 --> 02:30.442
with OOH, e-blasts, print and digital.

02:30.526 --> 02:35.573
Ain't nobody won't know about
the Democratic Church of America

02:35.656 --> 02:37.283
and its chosen prophet.

02:37.366 --> 02:39.243
[sighs]

02:40.911 --> 02:44.123
Prophets are servants.

02:44.206 --> 02:45.416
Of course.

02:45.499 --> 02:47.126
Sir, great point.

02:47.209 --> 02:49.336
We're just trying to ease people into it.

02:49.420 --> 02:54.800
No, no, no. We need to prepare America
for my ascension.

02:54.884 --> 02:57.761
-We must be honest. We must be direct.
-[claps hands]

02:57.845 --> 02:59.638
-I like "savior."
-[Firecracker] Mm.

02:59.722 --> 03:00.764
Or-or--

03:00.848 --> 03:02.057
Lord.

03:02.141 --> 03:03.851
Yes, I couldn't agree more, sir.

03:03.934 --> 03:06.520
-[Homelander] Mm.
-Religion is not about being meek.

03:06.604 --> 03:08.856
We should dominate

03:08.939 --> 03:11.191
the seven mountains of society,

03:11.275 --> 03:13.235
bring the Kingdom of Heaven to Earth.
Amen.

03:13.319 --> 03:16.071
-Amen.
-Amen. I love all that.

03:16.155 --> 03:17.364
So fucking dope.

03:17.448 --> 03:18.741
[Oh Father] Easter
is just around the corner.

03:18.824 --> 03:21.160
How perfect would it be
for your second coming

03:21.243 --> 03:24.288
to come on the day of Jesus' resurrection?

03:24.371 --> 03:27.291
Mm. Second coming?

03:27.374 --> 03:31.670
Let's be clear, I am not the son of God.

03:31.754 --> 03:34.298
Yeah, well, of course.

03:34.381 --> 03:38.552
Many people believe that Jesus
is both God incarnate and the son.

03:38.636 --> 03:39.845
Well, that's just confusing.

03:39.929 --> 03:42.890
I don't want my church
getting involved in all... that.

03:42.973 --> 03:43.974
[Firecracker] Exactly.

03:44.058 --> 03:46.101
Besides, if we pull up our timeline,

03:46.185 --> 03:48.562
you won't have...

03:48.646 --> 03:49.730
this.

03:49.813 --> 03:51.815
[hopeful music playing]

03:57.237 --> 03:59.198
[Homelander gasps]

04:01.241 --> 04:02.910
We're gonna drag our feet
because of a book?

04:02.993 --> 04:04.995
Not a book.

04:05.079 --> 04:07.414
The book.

04:07.498 --> 04:10.167
The Homelander Bible.

04:14.171 --> 04:15.214
Heavy.

04:15.798 --> 04:17.132
[quietly] What the fuck?

04:17.216 --> 04:20.344
It's got the Old Testament,
the New Testament,

04:20.427 --> 04:24.515
and the Brand New American Testament,

04:24.598 --> 04:26.934
written by A.I. trained on the works
of Pat Robertson.

04:27.017 --> 04:30.354
See, we need to pass the torch, sir,

04:30.437 --> 04:32.940
from Jesus to you.

04:33.023 --> 04:37.152
Sir, we don't get more than one chance
at a first impression.

04:37.236 --> 04:42.491
Are we really gonna rush
something this important?

04:42.574 --> 04:46.078
-We ain't Arby's, after all.
-No.

04:47.246 --> 04:49.540
We're the Cheesecake Factory.

04:51.750 --> 04:54.211
[sighs] Okay.

04:55.963 --> 04:57.589
We'll do it your way.

04:59.299 --> 05:01.677
Thank you.

05:01.760 --> 05:05.431
You do realize
this kind of sudden religious upheaval

05:05.514 --> 05:08.475
is likely to generate
widespread civil unrest?

05:08.559 --> 05:09.977
[Firecracker] Local law
should be able to handle the suburbs,

05:10.060 --> 05:13.272
but we could use extra hands
in major metros.

05:13.355 --> 05:15.691
Oh, let's recall all Supes
stationed overseas.

05:15.774 --> 05:18.402
American heroes should be
protecting America,

05:18.485 --> 05:20.404
-not Who-Gives-A-Fuckistan.
-Great idea.

05:20.487 --> 05:21.989
-[laughs]
-[phone vibrating]

05:23.949 --> 05:26.410
[suspenseful music playing]

05:28.871 --> 05:31.915
-Something wrong?
-Everything's peachy.

05:38.130 --> 05:39.465
[siren wailing in distance]

05:39.548 --> 05:43.594
[Reverend Dupree] Well, I can see why
they call this the city that never sleeps.

05:43.677 --> 05:45.763
How could you with all that racket?

05:46.847 --> 05:49.141
-You get used to it.
-You seem to have.

05:49.224 --> 05:50.726
City life seems to suit you.

05:50.808 --> 05:52.436
I guess.

05:54.813 --> 05:56.774
I was surprised you called, Reverend.

05:56.857 --> 05:58.776
Well, I was surprised you answered.

05:58.859 --> 06:01.695
It's been a while,
and, uh, I said things I regret.

06:01.779 --> 06:02.821
We both did.

06:06.408 --> 06:09.661
You remember when you used to
stop by the church after school?

06:09.745 --> 06:12.623
Use your powers
to light our candles? [laughs]

06:12.706 --> 06:14.541
I remember staying for supper.

06:15.292 --> 06:18.587
Oh, man, those Fish Fry Fridays.

06:18.670 --> 06:20.214
I never liked eating alone.

06:20.297 --> 06:23.842
Or were you making sure
I got at least one hot square a day?

06:26.929 --> 06:28.597
Reverend, is something the matter?

06:28.680 --> 06:33.102
I'm embarrassed to bug you
with all of this, but, um,

06:33.185 --> 06:35.562
the last couple of weeks have been rough.

06:35.646 --> 06:38.774
We've been bleeding congregants
to the Democratic Church of America,

06:38.857 --> 06:41.485
and what folks are sticking around,
they're scared.

06:42.236 --> 06:45.155
-Why?
-'Cause last Sunday, somebody, um,

06:45.239 --> 06:48.367
melted our stained glass window of Mary.

06:48.450 --> 06:50.536
-Melted it?
-Mm-hmm.

06:50.619 --> 06:53.956
It was our local Supe, Praying Mantis.

06:54.039 --> 06:56.792
He sprayed acid out of his butt.

06:56.875 --> 06:59.378
-I mean, his... his glands, his whatever.
-Yeah.

06:59.461 --> 07:01.630
-I know him.
-It was a message.

07:01.713 --> 07:05.884
I called the sheriff. I called the mayor.
I called half of Florida.

07:05.968 --> 07:07.594
You're all I got left.

07:07.678 --> 07:09.179
[sighs]

07:09.263 --> 07:10.931
Reverend, I don't know what I could do.

07:11.014 --> 07:13.517
[Reverend Dupree] Well,
you got to be able to do something.

07:13.600 --> 07:15.853
You're Homelander's right hand.

07:16.937 --> 07:20.941
Homelander's not too keen
on being challenged.

07:23.110 --> 07:25.612
Why not just pay
the franchise fee and join?

07:25.696 --> 07:27.739
Honey, we can barely afford
to pay our water bill.

07:29.283 --> 07:33.245
Besides, the Democratic Church of America?

07:33.328 --> 07:35.998
God does not favor
one nation over another.

07:36.081 --> 07:38.167
-Doesn't he, though? [chuckles]
-No.

07:38.250 --> 07:41.295
Name one way God's ever blessed Canada.
[chuckles]

07:44.381 --> 07:48.969
Just 'cause Homelander tells you
that the sky is red does not make it so.

07:52.264 --> 07:55.017
You still have that, uh,
that Jesus action figure?

07:55.100 --> 07:56.143
[Firecracker laughs]

07:56.226 --> 07:58.061
I'm surprised you remember that.

07:58.145 --> 08:00.147
How could I forget it? You carried it
with you everywhere you went.

08:00.230 --> 08:02.107
-[laughs]
-You almost wore the face off the thing.

08:02.191 --> 08:04.359
Do you still carry him?

08:06.195 --> 08:07.946
[gentle music playing]

08:09.781 --> 08:11.158
It's complicated.

08:11.241 --> 08:13.410
No, it's... I don't think it is.

08:14.494 --> 08:17.372
Homelander is a... he's a great American.

08:17.456 --> 08:21.668
He can stop bullets, he can fly,
and do amazing things.

08:21.752 --> 08:23.629
Those aren't miracles.

08:23.712 --> 08:26.256
And he is not God.

08:27.341 --> 08:31.053
If you're the same Misty Tucker Gray
that I taught the Bible to over fish,

08:31.136 --> 08:33.222
I think you know it, too.

08:37.643 --> 08:39.645
[groaning]

08:41.145 --> 08:42.981
[pants]

08:43.065 --> 08:44.650
[grunting]

08:48.987 --> 08:50.489
We ain't doing that again.

08:50.572 --> 08:53.116
[laughs] That's what you said
the last six times.

08:53.200 --> 08:55.327
No, I really mean it this time.

08:55.410 --> 08:56.620
[sighs]

08:58.872 --> 09:02.292
You seem a little out of it. Did you nut?

09:02.376 --> 09:03.794
'Cause usually you nut.

09:03.877 --> 09:05.045
[sighs]

09:07.673 --> 09:09.341
Were you baptized?

09:13.553 --> 09:15.347
Yeah, in front of half of Chestnut Hill.

09:15.430 --> 09:17.683
Governor Sproul did the honors.

09:17.766 --> 09:20.394
My family kept up appearances, of course.

09:20.477 --> 09:22.479
Then we never set foot in church again.

09:22.562 --> 09:25.399
I had lunch today with
the reverend who baptized me.

09:25.482 --> 09:28.527
He's been getting heat
to switch over to our church.

09:30.362 --> 09:32.698
You think Homelander might be open
to going easy on him?

09:32.781 --> 09:35.909
Just... give him a little more time?

09:35.993 --> 09:40.414
I wouldn't ask if it was just anybody,
but that man practically raised me.

09:42.124 --> 09:43.750
So you didn't nut?

09:46.753 --> 09:50.257
You know, this whole
Homelander as God shit, it's...

09:50.340 --> 09:51.717
it's fucking ridiculous.

09:52.801 --> 09:54.094
Really? You think so?

09:54.177 --> 09:58.056
If he's the second coming,
then what does that make me? Joseph?

09:58.140 --> 10:00.559
I mean, talk about
the biggest cuck in history.

10:00.642 --> 10:04.146
Man trades his best cow
to bag some hot-ass virgin,

10:04.229 --> 10:09.234
and then God comes and squirts
his baby gravy up her meat wallet.

10:09.318 --> 10:10.777
Fuck that.

10:11.778 --> 10:14.781
I guess I've been struggling
with where to place

10:14.865 --> 10:18.285
Homelander in my heart
in relation to Jesus and the Lord.

10:18.368 --> 10:20.787
Okay.

10:20.871 --> 10:22.331
Of course I worship Homelander.

10:22.414 --> 10:25.459
I mean, he's always been a god to me.

10:25.542 --> 10:26.960
Look, I'll tell you this.

10:27.044 --> 10:28.670
If there is a God...

10:30.464 --> 10:32.299
...sure as hell
didn't come out of my balls.

10:33.717 --> 10:35.552
-I got to go.
-Where you off to?

10:35.635 --> 10:36.970
L.A.

10:38.764 --> 10:40.307
I fucking hate L.A.

10:42.934 --> 10:43.935
[knock on door]

10:44.019 --> 10:45.395
[Firecracker] Homelander?

10:45.479 --> 10:47.189
[suspenseful music playing]

10:47.272 --> 10:48.648
Homelander?

10:48.732 --> 10:50.192
[soft whoosh]

10:51.610 --> 10:53.403
Hello?

10:56.156 --> 10:57.574
Does Homelander know you're here?

10:58.658 --> 10:59.826
Yeah, of course.

10:59.910 --> 11:03.413
Some of our church's followers
generously donated their milk

11:03.497 --> 11:05.082
for our savior's sustenance.

11:05.165 --> 11:08.126
I mean, he got to get this liquid gold
from somewhere, am I right? [laughing]

11:09.669 --> 11:10.670
You need something?

11:10.754 --> 11:12.172
Where's Homelander?

11:12.255 --> 11:14.341
Oh, uh, he didn't tell you?

11:14.424 --> 11:16.176
Yeah, he had to fly off to L.A.

11:16.259 --> 11:18.303
Strange he didn't mention anything.

11:18.387 --> 11:20.722
Well, I've been real busy
working for his glory,

11:20.806 --> 11:22.307
so not much time for chitchat.

11:22.391 --> 11:23.392
Of course.

11:23.475 --> 11:26.645
Look at us, a regular Peter and John,
just bearing witness

11:26.728 --> 11:27.979
-and spreading the gospel.
-[sighs]

11:28.063 --> 11:28.939
A real blessing.

11:29.022 --> 11:31.149
-Amen. A real...
-Amen.

11:31.233 --> 11:34.820
-...blessing.
-Oh, uh, by the way,

11:34.903 --> 11:39.658
after our meeting, I checked in
on the timeline of that Homelander Bible,

11:39.741 --> 11:43.703
and, uh, the printers were happy
to rush it to make Easter.

11:44.788 --> 11:47.040
Well, ain't you full of get-up-and-go.

11:47.124 --> 11:50.001
Thing is, they said it wasn't a problem.

11:50.085 --> 11:54.631
So, I wondered why you were so bent
on holding it up.

11:55.882 --> 11:57.676
I wasn't.

11:57.759 --> 12:01.138
See, I just wanted to make sure
everything was just right.

12:01.221 --> 12:05.934
Listen, if you are ever
feeling any doubts,

12:06.017 --> 12:07.769
come to me.

12:07.853 --> 12:10.188
I can be a warm shoulder
and a friendly ear.

12:11.356 --> 12:13.316
Well, bless your heart.

12:13.400 --> 12:15.318
[unsettling music playing]

12:15.402 --> 12:17.446
I'll do that.

12:18.822 --> 12:22.033
What'd you want to talk
to Homelander about?

12:22.117 --> 12:23.410
Maybe I can help.

12:23.493 --> 12:26.371
That is so kind of you.

12:27.831 --> 12:29.124
But it wasn't important.

12:36.006 --> 12:37.424
[knock on door]

12:39.968 --> 12:41.428
What's up?

12:41.511 --> 12:43.013
Um...

12:43.096 --> 12:45.640
Got a tip from our southeast stringer.

12:45.724 --> 12:49.478
Praying Mantis raided
half a dozen churches in Daytona.

12:49.561 --> 12:51.354
Was one of 'em Holy Baptist?

12:53.315 --> 12:57.777
The man upstairs wants us-- you--
to run with it top of show.

12:57.861 --> 13:01.990
He thinks with it being your home church
and all, it'll make a strong statement.

13:02.073 --> 13:04.075
So I'll have Chris load the new graphics?

13:05.494 --> 13:06.828
I got to finish getting ready.

13:06.912 --> 13:08.580
[somber music playing]

13:14.961 --> 13:17.088
-[rock music playing]
-♪ USA... ♪

13:17.172 --> 13:19.508
Welcome to Truthbomb.

13:19.591 --> 13:22.344
Our top story tonight's a personal one.

13:22.427 --> 13:25.138
It's the story of my hometown church,

13:25.222 --> 13:27.140
Holy Baptist of Daytona.

13:27.224 --> 13:28.934
It was the church I grew up in.

13:29.017 --> 13:31.478
Sang my hymns from the pews there
every Sunday.

13:32.812 --> 13:33.980
But that church...

13:38.443 --> 13:39.778
That church...

13:44.157 --> 13:45.617
That church...

13:48.912 --> 13:51.039
...has become

13:51.122 --> 13:55.460
a hotbed of Starlighter infestation.

13:55.544 --> 13:57.295
And my old pastor,

13:57.379 --> 14:02.342
Reverend Greg Dupree, has been infected

14:02.425 --> 14:05.762
by Starlight's seditious propaganda.

14:08.598 --> 14:09.599
Now...

14:12.352 --> 14:13.853
...I never told a soul this,

14:13.937 --> 14:19.651
but when I was a little girl, the reverend
regularly had me over for supper.

14:20.569 --> 14:21.695
Alone.

14:22.821 --> 14:23.863
No.

14:23.947 --> 14:26.324
Nothing ever happened to me, but...

14:26.408 --> 14:28.076
[sighs]

14:28.159 --> 14:33.623
I heard stories
about his "Fish Fry Fridays."

14:33.707 --> 14:37.627
And if that ain't code for child grooming,

14:37.711 --> 14:40.005
I don't know what is.

14:41.464 --> 14:43.675
How much longer

14:43.758 --> 14:48.221
are we gonna let
these institutional pedo churches

14:48.305 --> 14:50.223
diddle our babies?

14:52.475 --> 14:54.936
Americans deserve better.

14:58.023 --> 15:01.901
They deserve... Homelander.

15:03.862 --> 15:05.780
They deserve

15:05.864 --> 15:09.784
the Democratic Church of America.

15:12.370 --> 15:14.372
[unsettling music playing]

15:20.086 --> 15:21.588
[phone vibrates]

15:22.672 --> 15:24.215
[unsettling music playing]

15:24.299 --> 15:26.009
Something wrong?

15:26.092 --> 15:27.969
Everything's peachy.

15:31.348 --> 15:33.516
-Would you like some knee pads?
-I'm sorry?

15:33.600 --> 15:35.894
You're looking at me
like you want to suck my hog.

15:37.520 --> 15:39.898
So I'm asking if you would like
some knee pads.

15:39.981 --> 15:41.107
[stammers]

15:41.191 --> 15:42.567
[Homelander] Take it easy
on the little guy.

15:42.651 --> 15:44.110
He brought me Stan Edgar.

15:44.194 --> 15:45.737
[knuckles crack]

15:47.197 --> 15:49.366
Thank you, sir. Thank you.

15:49.449 --> 15:50.784
[dramatic music playing]

15:54.204 --> 15:56.164
[lighthearted music playing]

16:09.719 --> 16:14.140
Barry Gibb. B.G.
There's no Bee Gees without me.

16:14.224 --> 16:15.975
B.G. means the "Brothers Gibb."

16:16.059 --> 16:18.269
What, you think that falsetto
makes you boss?

16:18.353 --> 16:21.898
I think Saturday Night Fever
going platinum 16 times makes me boss.

16:21.981 --> 16:23.483
We made that album together.

16:23.566 --> 16:25.819
You're nothing without me and Maurice.

16:25.902 --> 16:27.946
Don't you dare bring Maurice into this!

16:28.029 --> 16:29.239
[scoffs]

16:29.322 --> 16:32.701
I don't know. It feels inauthentic
for Barry to move like this.

16:32.784 --> 16:33.910
[Adam] Oh, yeah?

16:36.621 --> 16:37.747
In what way?

16:37.831 --> 16:41.418
Egomaniacs like Barry
are-are really just insecure.

16:41.501 --> 16:43.920
I think he's threatened by Robin's talent.

16:44.003 --> 16:48.216
So, maybe he, uh, expresses that
by doing a barrel roll instead?

16:51.553 --> 16:53.888
Never mind. Sorry, I broke character.
I didn't mean to--

16:53.972 --> 16:55.765
Yeah.

16:55.849 --> 16:57.434
You need to apologize all right.

16:58.935 --> 17:01.354
For being a fucking genius.

17:01.438 --> 17:04.733
Are you fucking kidding me? A barrel roll?

17:04.816 --> 17:06.358
Holy shit.

17:07.569 --> 17:09.154
It's brilliant.

17:09.237 --> 17:12.115
Justin, I don't know who you are,

17:12.198 --> 17:14.367
or where you came from,
or anything about you,

17:14.451 --> 17:17.619
but, my God, if you are not
a fucking talent.

17:17.704 --> 17:18.829
-Wow, thank you.
-No.

17:20.665 --> 17:22.083
Thank you.

17:22.166 --> 17:23.835
Let's take ten, everybody.

17:23.917 --> 17:26.212
-[siren wailing in distance]
-[Adam sighs]

17:27.380 --> 17:28.673
All right.

17:30.717 --> 17:32.719
-Lay it on me, Justin.
-What do you mean?

17:32.802 --> 17:35.638
You're acting up there. Stop acting.

17:35.722 --> 17:37.432
Stop acting.

17:37.515 --> 17:41.436
Don't act. Don't.

17:41.519 --> 17:43.730
Because I don't need an actor.

17:44.898 --> 17:46.232
I need Barry Gibb.

17:46.316 --> 17:48.359
You're right, boss. I'm sorry.

17:48.443 --> 17:51.279
My process has been all over the map.
I just...

17:51.362 --> 17:52.947
This scene hits a little close to home.

17:53.031 --> 17:54.115
[sighs]

17:54.199 --> 17:56.618
All right, let me guess.
The egomaniac we're talking about,

17:56.701 --> 17:58.161
that's someone in your life?

17:58.244 --> 17:59.412
Someone I work with.

17:59.496 --> 18:02.081
In my... day job.

18:02.165 --> 18:03.166
All right. What are you doing? So quit.

18:03.249 --> 18:05.835
There's no way this gig is more important
than the fucking theater.

18:05.919 --> 18:07.170
I thought this guy was my brother,

18:07.253 --> 18:10.882
but he straight-up hijacked something
I did and took all the credit for it.

18:10.965 --> 18:12.342
All right.

18:14.344 --> 18:17.847
I've been trying to keep this
on the D.L., but...

18:17.931 --> 18:19.557
in addition to my theater work,

18:19.641 --> 18:22.352
I also happen to be
a massive feature director.

18:22.435 --> 18:24.020
Four Saturn Awards to prove it.

18:24.103 --> 18:26.773
So, I was working on this little film,
I don't know, you may have heard of it,

18:26.856 --> 18:28.691
called Dawn of the Seven.

18:28.775 --> 18:30.777
Billion dollar gross, but who's counting.

18:31.903 --> 18:35.156
There was this fucking guy, the Deep,

18:35.240 --> 18:40.036
he just kept upstaging everyone
with his trite, shitty improvs.

18:40.119 --> 18:41.746
I heard he's a real baby.

18:41.830 --> 18:44.916
He is a Jared Leto-level baby bitch.

18:44.999 --> 18:48.336
But you got to put people like that
in their place, right?

18:48.419 --> 18:52.257
So, whoever is upstaging you,
you fucking upstage them right back.

18:52.340 --> 18:53.758
-Okay?
-Yeah.

18:53.842 --> 18:54.843
All right.

18:54.926 --> 18:56.261
You got this, bubbeleh.

18:56.344 --> 18:58.471
[lighthearted music playing]

18:58.555 --> 19:01.140
[computer voice]
Testing. Testing. Bitch. Bitch.

19:01.224 --> 19:02.934
-So great you're here, bro.
-Alpha. Sigma. Beta.

19:03.017 --> 19:06.771
Yes, well, we need to meet young men
where they are

19:06.855 --> 19:09.566
if we plan to usher them
into the fold of our Lord.

19:09.649 --> 19:10.859
Mm. Totes McGotes.

19:10.942 --> 19:13.403
So, listen, you know, I've got some ideas

19:13.486 --> 19:16.239
about how to take this whole
church thing to the next level.

19:16.322 --> 19:17.323
Oh, yeah?

19:17.407 --> 19:20.660
So you know how communion wafers
taste like dried shit?

19:22.203 --> 19:24.455
What if they were Nilla wafers instead.

19:24.539 --> 19:25.957
Ah?

19:26.040 --> 19:28.668
Oh, yeah, and if you could
throw in a commandment

19:28.751 --> 19:31.796
about how it's not cool
to try and bone another bro's girl.

19:33.172 --> 19:35.967
We have that. That already exists.

19:36.050 --> 19:38.094
Great minds then, eh? [laughs]

19:38.177 --> 19:40.179
Point is, me and Homelander,
we go way back.

19:40.263 --> 19:41.681
I know what he likes, doesn't like,

19:41.764 --> 19:44.058
so you ever want to bounce
some ideas back--

19:44.142 --> 19:45.310
Don't listen to him, bro.

19:45.393 --> 19:47.854
Oh, shit!

19:47.937 --> 19:49.063
He talks.

19:49.147 --> 19:51.232
-No, he does not.
-He's not trying to help you.

19:51.316 --> 19:52.692
He's like those fish who suck on whales.

19:52.775 --> 19:54.569
[scoffs] You talking about a suckerfish?

19:54.652 --> 19:58.990
He latches onto every new Supe--
Starlight, me, Sage.

19:59.073 --> 20:02.452
He pretends he's the guy,
but he's not the guy. He's a joke.

20:02.535 --> 20:06.497
That smell on his breath? It's because
he's been clam diving, on clams.

20:06.581 --> 20:08.416
What? I have not done that.

20:08.499 --> 20:10.793
-I have definitely never done that.
-[Black Noir] Look, if you

20:10.877 --> 20:14.005
really want to impress Homelander,
bring me onstage for Easter.

20:14.088 --> 20:16.341
Homelander can heal me.
I'll get my voice back.

20:16.424 --> 20:17.967
And then, I'll fly.

20:18.927 --> 20:21.763
-You know I can fly, right?
-That's so fucking stupid, bro!

20:21.846 --> 20:24.849
Well, now, I'm gonna have to run this
by Homelander, but, uh,

20:24.933 --> 20:26.434
an honest to God faith healing?

20:26.517 --> 20:29.270
That's like a nine-point bump
with Pentecostals right there.

20:29.354 --> 20:32.315
[laughs] Goddamn.

20:35.193 --> 20:37.195
[lighthearted music playing]

20:48.748 --> 20:50.500
[Adam] There's my guy.

20:50.583 --> 20:52.460
Little pep in the step, huh?

20:53.753 --> 20:58.132
Sir, I did what you said,
and I upstaged that fuckhead at work.

20:58.216 --> 20:59.509
I'm proud of you.

20:59.592 --> 21:02.887
Now, that's exactly how I handled
that motherfucker Paul Rudd.

21:02.971 --> 21:04.180
He's not who you think he is.

21:04.263 --> 21:05.640
I appreciate the help, boss.

21:05.723 --> 21:07.350
