31:21.547 --> 31:23.215
What if it was Becca?

31:24.883 --> 31:26.468
You'd just let her die?

31:28.554 --> 31:30.556
[tense music playing]

31:31.974 --> 31:33.892
I did let her die.

31:34.977 --> 31:36.687
Look.

31:36.770 --> 31:39.523
I know that Homelander comes first.

31:39.607 --> 31:40.691
I really do.

31:40.774 --> 31:44.194
All I'm asking is that we try.

31:45.613 --> 31:47.573
Annie and Kimiko deserve that much.

31:49.033 --> 31:50.576
[garbage can clatters]

31:50.659 --> 31:52.244
Oi, Terror, no!

31:53.120 --> 31:56.290
Oi, get out of there.
Oh, bloody hell. Is that chocolate?

31:56.373 --> 31:58.167
Isn't chocolate bad for dogs?

31:58.250 --> 32:00.085
For a dog this old,
it's fucking lethal. Oi!

32:00.169 --> 32:03.213
Frenchie, you cunt!
Get me some hydrogen peroxide, would you?

32:03.297 --> 32:05.758
Okay, we have some in the first aid kit.
Give me one second.

32:05.841 --> 32:07.843
-What happened?
-You poisoned me fucking dog.

32:07.926 --> 32:10.638
-No, no, no, no, no, no, no.
-What's going on?

32:10.721 --> 32:12.097
Look, all you need is charcoal.

32:12.181 --> 32:13.474
-[Kimiko] We should call a vet.
-[Mother's Milk] They're gonna tell you

32:13.557 --> 32:14.767
-you need charcoal.
-[Hughie] Guys, we got this.

32:14.850 --> 32:16.894
-Just give us some room.
-I'll hold his mouth open, you pour.

32:16.977 --> 32:19.980
Right? On the count of three.
One, two, three.

32:20.064 --> 32:21.273
Sorry, buddy.

32:21.940 --> 32:23.108
There you go.

32:24.109 --> 32:26.153
[Butcher] That's a-- All right, all right.

32:26.236 --> 32:27.863
[Terror gagging, wheezing]

32:28.864 --> 32:30.282
-[Butcher] Oof. That's it.
-Ew.

32:30.366 --> 32:31.617
That's it. Good boy. You're all right.

32:31.700 --> 32:33.452
You're gonna be all right, boy.

32:35.287 --> 32:36.914
[sighs] Fucking hell.

32:41.001 --> 32:44.880
-Hey. You want some turkey?
-[Terror panting]

32:44.963 --> 32:48.467
[distorted] Well, first,
you got to fuck me.

32:48.550 --> 32:51.011
Then I'll give you the turkey.

32:55.974 --> 32:57.059
Oi.

32:58.519 --> 33:00.479
There he is, eh.

33:01.313 --> 33:03.941
Oi. Hey, were you
having a dream, were you?

33:04.024 --> 33:05.234
Was it a goody?

33:06.068 --> 33:07.945
[knock on door]

33:08.028 --> 33:09.113
How's he doing?

33:09.196 --> 33:11.031
[Butcher] Yeah, he's all right.

33:12.366 --> 33:14.535
Thank you for, uh...

33:14.618 --> 33:17.079
Yeah. It's all good.

33:21.417 --> 33:23.419
[gentle music playing]

33:27.631 --> 33:29.174
Oi.

33:29.258 --> 33:30.384
Hughie.

33:33.137 --> 33:35.514
Listen, uh...

33:35.597 --> 33:38.475
If we do find that V1,

33:38.559 --> 33:40.769
and if it don't fuck us, uh...

33:42.271 --> 33:43.939
...y-you can have some.

33:46.150 --> 33:49.653
For Annie and, uh... Kimiko.

33:49.737 --> 33:51.488
What about you?

33:53.866 --> 33:56.785
Oi, but as soon as Frenchie's
got that shite sorted,

33:56.869 --> 33:58.996
we're using it, all right? Ready or not.

34:04.752 --> 34:06.253
Ooh.

34:08.630 --> 34:10.132
[softly] Yeah.

34:12.842 --> 34:14.303
What you looking at?

34:16.096 --> 34:17.347
Nothing.

34:21.851 --> 34:25.938
And as for you, don't you ever
fucking do that to me again, all right?

34:26.774 --> 34:28.609
Good boy.

34:28.692 --> 34:33.697
Now, I caught Blondie trying to give
your wank-plush the boil wash,

34:33.781 --> 34:35.866
but I know how you love the crunchy goods.

34:35.949 --> 34:39.495
Yes, I do. I know how you love
those crunchy goods. Yeah.

34:42.790 --> 34:44.583
[squeaking rhythmically]

34:51.882 --> 34:56.637
You do realize this kind of sudden
religious upheaval is likely

34:56.719 --> 34:58.764
to generate widespread civil unrest?

34:58.847 --> 35:00.849
Local law can handle
the suburbs, but we could use

35:00.933 --> 35:02.059
extra hands in major metros.

35:02.142 --> 35:04.770
All right, we'll recall
all the Supes stationed overseas.

35:04.853 --> 35:07.731
American heroes should be
protecting America,

35:07.815 --> 35:10.025
not Who-Gives-A-Fuckistan.

35:10.108 --> 35:11.944
-[Firecracker laughs]
-Great idea.

35:12.027 --> 35:14.738
[intriguing music playing]

35:23.038 --> 35:25.040
-Where to?
-Crime analytics.

35:26.124 --> 35:27.501
[elevator bell chimes]

35:27.584 --> 35:29.211
[elevator doors slide closed]

35:31.004 --> 35:33.382
-That was thrilling, wasn't it?
-[elevator beeping steadily]

35:34.842 --> 35:37.094
What a bright future we have ahead of us.

35:37.886 --> 35:39.638
It was a real Guccione piss party.

35:40.722 --> 35:44.601
Imagine how much more exciting it'll be
when Homelander becomes immortal.

35:45.811 --> 35:46.937
Mm.

35:47.020 --> 35:49.356
Have you found the V1?

35:51.441 --> 35:52.442
No.

35:53.193 --> 35:55.654
Homelander hasn't gotten anything
out of Stan Edgar?

35:55.737 --> 35:58.907
No. But I haven't had a crack at him yet.

36:00.033 --> 36:01.034
[chuckles]

36:01.118 --> 36:03.328
-[elevator bell chimes]
-[doors slide open]

36:03.412 --> 36:05.330
[intriguing music playing]

36:06.623 --> 36:08.125
[doors slide closed]

36:08.208 --> 36:09.668
[door opens]

36:09.751 --> 36:12.546
Jesus, give me a little personal space,
will you, Garth?

36:12.629 --> 36:13.881
[groans]

36:13.964 --> 36:17.467
Twenty-four-seven agents must be hard
for someone so into scat play.

36:17.551 --> 36:19.011
You realize I do actually work?

36:19.094 --> 36:23.473
I was this close to convincing the FCC
to pull every broadcast license but VNN.

36:23.557 --> 36:26.560
Homelander feels this is more important.

36:26.643 --> 36:28.228
[sighs]

36:28.312 --> 36:30.230
What now?

36:30.314 --> 36:31.815
The president and I
stand by this decision.

36:31.899 --> 36:33.942
We need our American Supes
here in America.

36:34.026 --> 36:35.277
[man over phone speaking angrily]

36:35.360 --> 36:38.405
Well, isn't it kind of sort of
your fault for being invaded?

36:38.488 --> 36:40.532
You might as well have been
wearing a short skirt.

36:40.616 --> 36:43.201
Man, those Ukrainians sure have
a fucking mouth on them.

36:44.286 --> 36:46.788
Remember, you're doing the Lord's work.

36:46.872 --> 36:49.124
Word's out, Vought's stock is tanking.

36:49.207 --> 36:52.044
The international markets
are in freefall, and you're not

36:52.127 --> 36:55.172
-the least bit concerned?
-It's not about what I think.

36:55.255 --> 36:56.632
It's what the man wants.

36:58.133 --> 36:59.885
It's always what the man wants.

36:59.968 --> 37:02.179
[dramatic music playing]

37:05.515 --> 37:07.100
You want a drink?

37:07.184 --> 37:09.394
So, we're at the Climate Change Summit
in Reykjavík,

37:09.478 --> 37:12.814
when the Swiss chancellor says
we should all race our Gulfstreams.

37:12.898 --> 37:15.359
The amount of CO2 we splooged out?

37:15.442 --> 37:19.905
The air was chewy the next day, lolz.
[laughs]

37:22.574 --> 37:24.952
Come on. What do you want from me, Sage?

37:25.035 --> 37:26.828
What makes you think
I want anything from you?

37:26.912 --> 37:29.790
You haven't called me the poster child
for late-term abortion once today.

37:29.873 --> 37:32.167
Truth be told, you're not the one I want.

37:33.251 --> 37:35.712
I know you know what Homelander's doing.

37:35.796 --> 37:38.507
-[Bashley] He's going after the V1.
-Wait, what?!

37:38.590 --> 37:40.342
And if he gets any--

37:40.425 --> 37:42.427
-He lives forever.
-What is V1?

37:42.511 --> 37:45.055
And what do you mean
Homelander lives forever? [gasps]

37:45.138 --> 37:47.557
I've done what I can to make sure
he doesn't find any.

37:47.641 --> 37:49.935
How do you know about this and I don't?

37:50.018 --> 37:52.020
Have you two been talking without me?

37:53.105 --> 37:56.066
Homelander is an open baby book,
but Soldier Boy is tricky.

37:56.149 --> 37:57.442
I need you to read his mind.

37:57.526 --> 37:59.569
What he knows, where they're headed next,

37:59.653 --> 38:03.615
and most importantly, if Soldier Boy
is warming up to his sadistic rugrat.

38:05.117 --> 38:06.243
Okay. I'm in.

38:06.326 --> 38:08.120
The fuck you are.

38:08.203 --> 38:10.831
-We're not conspiring against Homelander.
-[Bashley] Hey.

38:10.914 --> 38:13.458
Don't forget the Aung San Suu Kyi quote
tramp stamped on our ass.

38:14.751 --> 38:16.211
"The only real prison is fear."

38:16.294 --> 38:18.880
-No, the only real prison is prison.
-Ashley--

38:18.964 --> 38:21.925
What do you think happens to you if I die?

38:22.009 --> 38:23.427
I'm not about to risk my neck

38:23.510 --> 38:26.304
because I let an overgrown boil
do my thinking for me.

38:27.389 --> 38:29.224
Okay, fine. Just stay.

38:29.307 --> 38:30.934
Why? So you can play more mind games?

38:31.018 --> 38:33.395
You gave me your answer. I heard you.

38:33.478 --> 38:36.273
Now, don't make me drink alone.

38:36.356 --> 38:38.400
[dramatic music playing]

38:38.483 --> 38:40.902
[Ashley] I'm starving. Are you starving?

38:40.986 --> 38:43.488
I'd kill for a chalupa right now.

38:43.572 --> 38:45.032
[Bashley] I'd kill for a big, juicy dick.

38:45.115 --> 38:46.408
Hey, we should call Gavin.

38:46.491 --> 38:49.202
His girth was amazing,
and, oh, man, the amount of spunk

38:49.286 --> 38:51.455
he shot back here,
we looked like Pepé Le Pew.

38:51.538 --> 38:54.291
We are not booty-calling
my high school boyfriend.

38:54.374 --> 38:56.418
[Bashley] But he was so sweet.
And Mom loved him, remember?

38:56.501 --> 38:58.712
Yeah, well, Mom's dead,
so she doesn't get a say,

38:58.795 --> 39:00.922
-and neither do you.
-What happened to her?

39:01.006 --> 39:02.549
Cancer.

39:02.632 --> 39:04.301
My grandmother, too.

39:04.384 --> 39:07.471
What was she like? Your mother?

39:08.555 --> 39:11.349
Tiny. [laughs] And terrifying.

39:12.142 --> 39:14.936
This one bitch, Harper Hewitt,
used to make fun of my nose,

39:15.020 --> 39:18.023
so my mom tells Mr. Hewitt
that Mrs. Hewitt

39:18.106 --> 39:21.401
has been railing the UPS guy,
which she was.

39:21.485 --> 39:24.613
That was Mom,
bringing a nuke to a knife fight.

39:27.949 --> 39:29.618
So, they moved.

39:29.701 --> 39:31.495
And the rest of kindergarten was no sweat.

39:32.162 --> 39:36.625
My folks shot me up with V,
thinking I'd be a meal ticket.

39:36.708 --> 39:39.086
And then, my power
turned out to be smarts.

39:39.169 --> 39:40.754
Which is the worst fucking one.

39:40.837 --> 39:42.881
Try knowing what everyone
really thinks of you all day.

39:42.964 --> 39:43.965
Ooh, trust me.

39:44.049 --> 39:47.636
The thing people hate
more than just about anything

39:47.719 --> 39:49.096
is feeling stupid.

39:49.179 --> 39:53.892
So, when a three-year-old
corrects your grammar or, oh, tells them

39:53.975 --> 39:57.020
their "life dream yogurt shop"
is doomed to fail,

39:57.104 --> 39:58.939
they start to hate you, too.

39:59.022 --> 40:00.023
Least my parents did.

40:00.107 --> 40:02.025
So they dumped me at my grandma's.

40:02.609 --> 40:04.528
But Grandma,

40:04.611 --> 40:08.198
she was the only one
who ever thought it was a gift.

40:08.281 --> 40:11.243
I would quote Othello to her
word for word,

40:11.326 --> 40:14.830
and-and... [sighs] she'd clap

40:14.913 --> 40:16.790
and laugh her big laugh.

40:19.501 --> 40:22.754
I'm still so pissed she is gone.

40:23.839 --> 40:26.591
I used to want to be like my mom.

40:26.675 --> 40:29.511
Strong. Pushy as fuck.

40:29.594 --> 40:31.388
Didn't take shit from anyone.

40:31.471 --> 40:33.056
You still can.

40:34.307 --> 40:35.725
If you help me.

40:38.270 --> 40:39.771
Fuck you.

40:39.855 --> 40:41.606
You knew about my mom the whole time.

40:41.690 --> 40:43.775
You drew it out of me
just to soften me up.

40:43.859 --> 40:47.028
-Did it work?
-No. This is my fucking problem with you.

40:47.112 --> 40:49.239
I know you've been working
some big plan all year.

40:49.322 --> 40:53.076
How am I supposed to trust you if I'm just
a pawn in your fucked-up chess game?

40:53.160 --> 40:54.536
All right.

40:55.537 --> 40:57.289
If I tell you, will you help me?

40:58.373 --> 41:00.125
I would heavily consider it.

41:00.208 --> 41:04.296
Helping Homelander take control
of the country is phase one.

41:04.379 --> 41:07.048
It was only ever the beginning.
Phase two is the end.

41:07.132 --> 41:09.259
-The end of what?
-The world.

41:10.343 --> 41:12.846
After this Supe-killing virus
is released--

41:12.929 --> 41:15.682
-Wait, you want it released?
-Oh, you bet I do.

41:16.641 --> 41:21.688
After Supes realize humans are behind it,
all hell will break loose.

41:21.771 --> 41:25.066
Supes butchering humans,
virus butchering Supes.

41:25.150 --> 41:28.069
-Oh, fucking World War Supe.
-I don't believe you.

41:28.153 --> 41:30.030
Swear on my grandma's soul.

41:30.113 --> 41:32.073
Why would you possibly want that?

41:32.157 --> 41:36.286
'Cause I'll be watching from
my cozy bunker outside Colorado Springs.

41:36.369 --> 41:41.625
And when it's all over,
I can read all day every day,

41:41.708 --> 41:44.336
no one bothering me.

41:44.419 --> 41:47.088
Nothing but peace and quiet forever.

41:47.172 --> 41:49.549
[ominous music playing]

41:49.633 --> 41:51.927
Which is why Homelander can't survive.

41:52.010 --> 41:55.722
God, that needy asshole
would never give me a moment's rest.

41:55.805 --> 41:57.390
Yeah, defeats the whole purpose.

41:57.474 --> 42:01.061
Don't worry. You're invited to my bunker.

42:01.978 --> 42:03.605
You, too, Ashley.

42:06.149 --> 42:08.068
[Bashley] Fuck.

42:10.528 --> 42:13.406
-Would you like some knee pads?
-Sorry? What?

42:13.490 --> 42:16.201
You're looking at me
like you want to suck my hog.

42:18.036 --> 42:20.538
So I'm asking you if you would like
some knee pads.

42:21.289 --> 42:22.958
[Homelander] Go easy on the little guy.

42:23.041 --> 42:25.335
-He brought me Stan Edgar.
-[Deep] Thank you, sir.

42:25.418 --> 42:27.212
[Homelander] You may leave.

42:27.295 --> 42:29.005
[triumphant music playing]

42:38.014 --> 42:39.641
What crawled up your shithole?

42:39.724 --> 42:41.017
No idea what you mean.

42:41.101 --> 42:43.603
When you're pissy,

42:43.687 --> 42:46.314
you tend to make
everybody else's lives pissy, too.

42:46.982 --> 42:49.734
Stan Edgar still stonewalling you?

42:49.818 --> 42:51.319
I've talked to him three times now.

42:51.403 --> 42:55.573
Says he has no idea where the V1 is.
Heart rate steady as a rock.

42:55.657 --> 42:56.950
I'm starting to believe him.

42:57.033 --> 42:59.869
That slippery fuck
used to fetch my cocaine.

43:02.914 --> 43:05.542
You know what? I have an idea.

43:08.003 --> 43:10.422
Why don't I take a crack at him?

43:11.589 --> 43:13.091
What, you don't trust me?

43:13.174 --> 43:17.137
Well, you did lock me in a room
with nuclear material

43:17.220 --> 43:19.806
and, uh, tried to stop me getting the V1,

43:19.889 --> 43:25.061
so I'm sure you can understand
my hesitance.

43:25.145 --> 43:28.023
You could've killed me at Fort Harmony,
but you didn't.

43:28.106 --> 43:30.442
-Maybe I feel like I owe you.
-Or maybe you're lying.

43:30.525 --> 43:31.484
Maybe.

43:34.738 --> 43:36.531
[inhales deeply]

43:37.365 --> 43:38.742
Give me an hour.

43:39.617 --> 43:41.369
I'll meet you at Edgar's cell.

43:41.453 --> 43:43.413
[dramatic music playing]

43:43.496 --> 43:45.498
[urinating]

43:50.962 --> 43:56.509
[Soldier Boy] My, my, how the mighty
have fucked themselves square in the ass.

43:57.344 --> 43:58.845
Don't shit where you eat, Stan.

43:58.928 --> 44:00.930
So, you've called in reinforcements.

44:01.014 --> 44:03.183
I wanted to see the prick
that sold me out to the Reds.

44:03.266 --> 44:05.643
It wasn't personal.
It was a business decision.

44:05.727 --> 44:08.563
We had your replacement model on the way.

44:08.646 --> 44:12.859
Even as a toddler, Homelander showed
more promise than you ever did.

44:13.985 --> 44:16.237
Not that it amounted to much.

44:16.321 --> 44:19.908
When have you ever done anything

44:19.991 --> 44:22.994
remotely interesting or original?

44:23.078 --> 44:26.998
My power is absolute, Stan.

44:27.082 --> 44:30.085
At heights no one's even dreamed of.

44:30.168 --> 44:32.003
I'd call that pretty fucking original.

44:32.087 --> 44:33.713
Nothing that the lowest speck

44:33.797 --> 44:37.217
of this pointless species
couldn't have thought of,

44:37.300 --> 44:40.345
were they to be granted
your level of power.

44:40.428 --> 44:43.681
Why am I still alive?

44:43.765 --> 44:46.726
Oh, because you're useful, Stan.

44:47.727 --> 44:50.313
-And I always wanted a pet.
-Perhaps.

44:50.397 --> 44:53.650
Or is it because you are so desperate
for daddy figures

44:53.733 --> 44:57.821
that you can't even bring yourself
to kill the ones who hate you.

44:57.904 --> 45:01.282
At least that's something
he and I have in common.

45:01.908 --> 45:03.910
Do you want to die, Stan?

45:09.374 --> 45:10.375
[Soldier Boy] Jesus.

45:10.458 --> 45:12.961
You could get pregnant
with all the eye-fucking.

45:14.421 --> 45:15.922
Tempe, Arizona.

45:16.005 --> 45:17.507
Is that supposed to mean something?

45:17.590 --> 45:19.759
Well, I had the eggheads
in crime analytics

45:19.843 --> 45:23.388
track down your granddaughter, Zoe,

45:23.471 --> 45:24.806
and her dad.

45:24.889 --> 45:26.433
They're in Tempe, Arizona.

45:26.516 --> 45:28.685
[tense music playing]

45:29.269 --> 45:31.020
So...

45:31.104 --> 45:33.731
where is the V1?

45:35.275 --> 45:38.695
As I told you, I genuinely don't know.

45:44.617 --> 45:46.995
But...

45:47.078 --> 45:48.913
I may know someone who does.

45:48.997 --> 45:51.875
You should go and see
Mister Marathon in L.A.

45:52.959 --> 45:57.589
He's always had an intense interest
in Vought's history.

45:57.672 --> 46:00.758
It should be a delightful reunion.

46:00.842 --> 46:02.385
[suspenseful music playing]

46:04.262 --> 46:06.431
-[♪ Rosemary Clooney sings
"Hooray for Hollywood"]
-♪ Hooray for Hollywood ♪

46:06.514 --> 46:09.058
♪ That screwy, ballyhooey Hollywood ♪

46:09.142 --> 46:11.603
-[siren wailing in distance]
-♪ Go out and try your luck ♪

46:11.686 --> 46:13.354
♪ You might be Donald Duck ♪

46:13.438 --> 46:15.398
♪ Hooray for Hollywood ♪♪

46:15.482 --> 46:18.109
[Mister Marathon] Homelander,
it is really, uh, really good to see you.

46:18.193 --> 46:20.737
Um, why-- [stammers] Uh, you know,
what-what brings you by?

46:20.820 --> 46:23.281
-Relax. We're just here to talk.
-Yeah, yeah, great, awesome.

46:23.364 --> 46:25.617
And Soldier Boy, wow. Big fan, sir.

46:25.700 --> 46:28.203
I actually, uh, popped my cherry
in your Underoos.

46:28.870 --> 46:30.079
Nice.

46:30.163 --> 46:31.623
So you were part of The Seven?

46:31.706 --> 46:34.709
Uh, I was, I was. You know, until this one
replaced me with A-Train.

46:34.792 --> 46:36.085
Check it out. Come on.

46:37.170 --> 46:38.922
Well, you're only the world's fastest man

46:39.005 --> 46:42.175
as long as you're the world's fastest man,
Champ, and you got slow.

46:42.258 --> 46:45.762
It was one race. You never gave me
the chance to win it back, boss.

46:45.845 --> 46:47.680
[intriguing music playing]

46:49.682 --> 46:51.017
Hey, check this one out.

46:52.227 --> 46:53.520
Grossed 35 mil.

46:53.603 --> 46:55.063
On a $200 million budget.

46:55.146 --> 46:57.398
-These aren't even Vought films.
-What's the difference?

46:57.482 --> 47:00.318
These were made
where washed-up Supes go to die.

